## Worth knowing before you build on it

Around a quarter of the entries carry `"verify": true`, which means nobody has confirmed the
link or the description. They were inferred from a name in a set of private notes. If you
reuse this data, carry that flag through and show it to your users — presenting an unverified
guess as a checked fact is the one thing this project is trying not to do.

